.TH SCRCPYVNCSERVER 1 "" "TigerVNC" "TigerVNC Manual"
.SH NAME
scrcpyvncserver \- TigerVNC server bridging scrcpy H.264 streams with zero transcoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scrcpyvncserver
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B scrcpyvncserver -version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scrcpyvncserver
bridges an Android device running
.B scrcpy-server
to VNC viewers using the RFB Open H.264 encoding (encoding 50) without
host-side decoding, color-space conversion, or re-encoding.
.PP
It connects directly to the local ADB daemon (127.0.0.1:5037 by default)
via \fBhost:transport:<serial>\fP and \fBlocalabstract:scrcpy\fP with
\fBTCP_NODELAY\fP enabled, strips scrcpy's 12-byte packet header, and uses
scatter-gather I/O to prepend RFB Open H.264 headers directly
to the raw Annex-B NAL payload.
.PP
Viewers must support Open H.264 encoding (50). To follow Android display
resizes, they must also support DesktopSize (\-223) or ExtendedDesktopSize
(\-308). ContinuousUpdates (\-313) lets the server stream frames without
waiting for individual update requests. With an H.264-enabled
\fBvncviewer\fP(1), use \fB\-AutoSelect=0 \-PreferredEncoding=H.264\fP.
.SH OPTIONS
Parameters can be specified as \fB\-\fIParam\fR, \fB\-\fIParam\fP=0\fR,
or \fB\-\fIParam\fP=\fIvalue\fR. Run \fBscrcpyvncserver \-h\fP for the full
parameter list.
.TP
.BI \-ScrcpyServer " path"
Use this server JAR when launching scrcpy on the selected Android device.
If omitted, the server checks \fBSCRCPY_SERVER_PATH\fP and standard
installation paths.
.TP
.BI \-ScrcpyVersion " version"
Specify the server version. In attach mode, specify this for versions
older than 3.3.1 to select the correct control protocol.
.TP
.B \-Attach
Connect to an existing scrcpy server configured with forward tunneling,
H.264 video, audio disabled, and codec and frame metadata enabled. Match
its control, dummy byte, and device metadata settings. Use
\fB\-ScrcpySocket\fP or \fB\-Scid\fP to select its socket.
.TP
.BI \-HostsFile " path"
Apply IP access rules to TCP listeners, including systemd-activated
listeners. Connections that require interactive approval are rejected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vncviewer (1),
.BR x0vncserver (1),
.BR w0vncserver (1)
